    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d612-a3">

                <pb facs="1128" n="1004" xml:id="pg1004"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 73.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr.
                            de Giers.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-12-05"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 5 (17),
                            1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your two notes of the 1 (13) instant, the one relating to the case of
                    Henry Pinkos and the other to that of Marx Wilczynski, both American citizens of
                    the Jewish faith.</p>
                <p>In view of the conference which I had with your excellency on those and kindred
                    matters on yesterday, I do not deem it necessary at present to make further
                    reply to said notes than to say that I will forward copies thereof, as well as a
                    report of said conference, to the Secretary of State at Washington, and await
                    his instructions.</p>
                <p>With the renewed, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN W. FOSTER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
